{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "983d9021-a163-44bb-ac1e-761e869bb0a6",
    "name": "PAIGS WildID -- API",
    "description": "Manual test collection for the PAIGS WildID backend.\n\nUpdated 2026-09-24: added the 'End-to-end (Orchestration)' folder covering POST /runs/{id}/execute (build-order item 9) and reference database publishing, so the full Stage 1-11 pipeline can be exercised from Postman, not just Stage 0 import.\n\nSetup:\n1. From backend/, run: uvicorn app.main:app --reload\n2. Import the PAIGS environment (postman/PAIGS.postman_environment.json) alongside this collection and select it.\n3. 'Happy path' and 'Errors' cover Stage 0 (Import) only -- run 'Happy path' top to bottom first, it captures run_id into the environment. 'Errors' can be run independently, except 'Patch run - rejects empty label', which reuses run_id.\n4. 'End-to-end (Orchestration)' exercises the full pipeline via POST /runs/{id}/execute -- run it top to bottom, in its own pass (it publishes a reference database as a side effect, which is process-wide state that would change what later Stage 0/Errors requests see if interleaved with those folders).\n\nTest data lives in postman/test-data/ (copies of backend/tests/fixtures/*.ab1, a plain-text file for exercising the extension-rejection case, and reference.fasta -- a single-entry reference database whose sequence is 3100.ab1's own real trimmed output, extracted from backend/tests/test_api_execute.py, guaranteeing a clean 100%-identity BLAST hit for the end-to-end 'completes' request).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
